  "guide": {
    "purpose": "Drizzle 1.0 for queries and migrations. The `Database` service hands you a Drizzle client whose queries are Effects, so `yield* db.select().from(note)` works inside `Effect.gen`. `DatabaseLayer` in `packages/db` builds the client from the database binding. It comes with a `note` table and a notes demo on `/app`.",
    "service": {
      "name": "Database",
      "file": "packages/core/src/Database.ts",
      "errors": []
    },
    "limits": [
      "`drizzle-orm` and `drizzle-kit` are pinned to a 1.0 release candidate, the version under Dependencies ([why](../decisions/0002-drizzle-rc-pin.md))."
    ]
  },
  "transforms": [
    {
      "name": "addImport",
      "args": {
        "file": "apps/web/src/server/layers.ts",
        "import": "WorkerEnvLive",
        "from": "./cloudflare"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "addLayer",
      "args": {
        "file": "apps/web/src/server/layers.ts",
        "import": "DatabaseLayer",
        "from": "@repo/db",
        "layer": "DatabaseLayer.pipe(Layer.provide(WorkerEnvLive))"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "appendAgentsSection",
      "args": {
        "id": "orm",
        "content": "## Queries and migrations (Drizzle)\n\n- `Database` (`packages/core/src/Database.ts`) holds a Drizzle client whose queries are Effects. `DatabaseLayer` (`packages/db/src/layer.ts`) provides it and the repositories built on it, such as `NotesLive` (`packages/db/src/notes.ts`, for the `Notes` service in `packages/core`). Add a repository the same way and merge it into `DatabaseLayer`.\n- Map a query's failure to the service's tagged error (`Effect.mapError(notesUnavailable)`), so callers get a typed error rather than a driver error.\n- Tables live in `packages/db/src/schema.ts` (Better Auth's in `auth-schema.ts`).\n- Migrations in `packages/db/drizzle/` are generated by drizzle-kit: never edit, rename or delete one. To change the database, change the schema and generate a new migration.\n- Test logic against a test layer, not a database: a program that needs `Notes` gets an in-memory `Notes` layer in `packages/core/test/notes.test.ts`; do the same for a repository you add. Check the queries themselves under `pnpm dev`."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "appendAgentsSection",
      "args": {
        "id": "orm-migrate",
        "content": "- After changing the tables, run `pnpm db:generate` (it writes a migration), then `pnpm db:migrate`."
      },
      "when": {"database": ["postgres"]}
    },
    {
      "name": "appendAgentsSection",
      "args": {
        "id": "orm-migrate",
        "content": "- After changing the tables, run `pnpm db:generate` (it writes a migration), then `pnpm db:migrate`."
      },
      "when": {"database": ["d1"], "infra": ["none"]}
    },
    {
      "name": "appendAgentsSection",
      "args": {
        "id": "orm-migrate",
        "content": "- After changing the tables, run `pnpm db:generate` (it writes a migration). The next `pnpm dev` applies it to the local D1 and `pnpm run deploy` to the stage's; `pnpm db:migrate` is not used with Alchemy."
      },
      "when": {"database": ["d1"], "infra": ["alchemy"]}
    },
    {
      "name": "appendAgentsSection",
      "args": {
        "id": "orm-d1-flat",
        "content": "- On D1, `pnpm db:migrate` copies them into `packages/db/migrations/` (the flat layout wrangler applies) before applying them; that directory is generated too."
      },
      "when": {
        "database": [
          "d1"
        ],
        "infra": [
          "none"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
